WEBVTT

1
00:00:36.125 --> 00:00:38.625
<b>In the previous verse, Arjuna asked –</b>

2
00:00:38.625 --> 00:00:39.875
<b>O Krishna,</b>

3
00:00:39.875 --> 00:00:44.041
<b>you were born after the sun god Vivasvan?</b>

4
00:00:44.041 --> 00:00:50.166
<b>Then how was it possible that you</b>
<b> yourself gave him this knowledge of yoga?</b>

5
00:00:50.166 --> 00:00:54.250
<b>Here Arjuna was questioning Krishna's age.</b>

6
00:00:54.250 --> 00:00:57.291
<b>Now in this fifth verse of the fourth chapter,</b>

7
00:00:57.291 --> 00:01:00.166
<b>Lord Krishna is answering this.</b>

8
00:01:05.083 --> 00:01:09.291
<b>Answering Arjuna's question, </b>
<b>Lord Krishna says that</b>

9
00:01:09.291 --> 00:01:10.416
<b>O Arjuna,</b>

10
00:01:10.416 --> 00:01:13.500
<b>you and I have taken many births.</b>

11
00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:18.125
<b>The only difference is that I remember</b>
<b>all those births, </b>

12
00:01:18.125 --> 00:01:19.333
<b>but</b>

13
00:01:19.333 --> 00:01:21.500
<b>you don't.</b>

14
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:27.958
<b>What Lord Krishna means by this is </b>
<b>that he was not born just a few years ago.</b>

15
00:01:27.958 --> 00:01:30.916
<b>He existed from time immemorial,</b>

16
00:01:30.916 --> 00:01:33.875
<b>even then, when this universe was created,</b>

17
00:01:33.875 --> 00:01:36.333
<b>and he also remembers the event</b>

18
00:01:36.333 --> 00:01:40.916
<b>when he himself gave this knowledge </b>
<b>to the sun god Vivasvan.</b>

19
00:01:40.916 --> 00:01:41.833
<b>Also,</b>

20
00:01:41.833 --> 00:01:43.416
<b>Lord Krishna says,</b>

21
00:01:43.416 --> 00:01:48.333
<b>that not only him but Arjuna has also </b>
<b>existed through countless births.</b>

22
00:01:48.333 --> 00:01:51.583
<b>Here the spiritual form of </b>
<b>Arjuna is being talked about.</b>

23
00:01:51.583 --> 00:01:57.250
<b>This is the difference between Lord Krishna's </b>
<b>supreme existence and all of us.</b>

24
00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.916
<b>Krishna remembers the entire past,</b>

25
00:01:59.916 --> 00:02:05.000
<b>but souls like Arjuna and us </b>
<b>don't remember any of this.</b>

26
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.416
<b>Why is this so?</b>

27
00:02:06.416 --> 00:02:09.541
<b>This question must have arisen in your mind.</b>

28
00:02:09.541 --> 00:02:10.750
<b>So have patience,</b>

29
00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.875
<b>the answer to this will also come later.</b>

30
00:02:12.875 --> 00:02:14.500
<b>But one thing is clear</b>

31
00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:20.250
<b>that from this we get a glimpse of the unique and incomparable nature of Lord Krishna.</b>

32
00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:23.208
<b>Here Krishna also indicates to Arjuna</b>

33
00:02:23.208 --> 00:02:30.041
<b>how he manifests in his many incarnations </b>
<b>in different ages and eras.</b>

34
00:02:30.041 --> 00:02:33.958
<b>Krishna's body is completely divine and spiritual,</b>

35
00:02:33.958 --> 00:02:40.791
<b>as a result of which even if he takes different incarnations, his body does not change.</b>

36
00:02:40.791 --> 00:02:45.708
<b>Whereas individual souls like Arjuna and </b>
<b>us are situated in material bodies,</b>

37
00:02:45.708 --> 00:02:51.208
<b>and this body keeps changing </b>
<b>constantly with each new birth.</b>

38
00:02:51.208 --> 00:02:57.666
<b>And it is due to this reason that we do not </b>
<b>remember our past thoughts and events.</b>

39
00:02:57.666 --> 00:02:59.916
<b>In the forthcoming chapters and verses</b>

40
00:02:59.916 --> 00:03:02.791
<b>there is detailed knowledge about </b>
<b>the nature of Lord Krishna,</b>

41
00:03:02.791 --> 00:03:07.125
<b>but here just take this indication </b>
<b>that Lord Krishna is omniscient,</b>

42
00:03:07.125 --> 00:03:08.833
<b>he knows everything.</b>

43
00:03:08.833 --> 00:03:10.500
<b>His glory is immeasurable,</b>

44
00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:15.541
<b>and in front of him we are just an </b>
<b>insignificant individual soul.</b>

45
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.958
<b>I remember not only my own,</b>

46
00:03:22.958 --> 00:03:29.875
<b>but also Arjuna's and all of your previous births.</b>

47
00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:32.166
<b>I also know that</b>

48
00:03:32.166 --> 00:03:39.916
<b>perhaps questions and doubts must </b>
<b>be arising in your mind at this time?</b>

49
00:03:39.916 --> 00:03:42.041
<b>Have patience,</b>

50
00:03:42.041 --> 00:03:48.375
<b>there is still a lot of depth in this</b>
<b>ocean of spiritual knowledge.</b>

51
00:03:48.375 --> 00:03:54.333
<b>As we move forward, everything </b>
<b>will gradually become clear.</b>

52
00:03:54.333 --> 00:03:57.291
<b>But think about one thing?</b>

53
00:03:57.291 --> 00:04:04.083
<b>Why did this doubt or disbelief arise?</b>

54
00:04:04.083 --> 00:04:11.541
<b>Because perhaps you have not </b>
<b>personally experienced this.</b>

55
00:04:11.541 --> 00:04:13.833
<b>And for this reason,</b>

56
00:04:13.833 --> 00:04:18.375
<b>the mind immediately raised doubt.</b>

57
00:04:18.375 --> 00:04:22.833
<b>This is what happens in personal life,</b>

58
00:04:22.833 --> 00:04:31.083
<b>we look at things we have not experienced </b>
<b>ourselves with disbelief.</b>

59
00:04:31.083 --> 00:04:33.541
<b>Similarly,</b>

60
00:04:33.541 --> 00:04:40.166
<b>we meet many people whose abilities </b>
<b>are far greater than ours.</b>

61
00:04:40.166 --> 00:04:45.583
<b>Sometimes seeing them, </b>
<b>jealousy arises in the mind.</b>

62
00:04:45.583 --> 00:04:47.791
<b>Remember,</b>

63
00:04:47.791 --> 00:04:51.333
<b>this is an opportunity for inspiration,</b>

64
00:04:51.333 --> 00:04:53.666
<b>not for envy.</b>

65
00:04:53.666 --> 00:04:58.083
<b>It can also be thought of in this way</b>

66
00:04:58.083 --> 00:05:02.250
<b>that if someone else can do it,</b>

67
00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:06.875
<b>then it means that it is possible to do so.</b>

68
00:05:06.875 --> 00:05:11.125
<b>If you want, you can also do it.</b>

69
00:05:11.125 --> 00:05:12.208
<b>Envy</b>

70
00:05:12.208 --> 00:05:14.125
<b>and disbelief,</b>

71
00:05:14.125 --> 00:05:18.666
<b>both of these are enemies of </b>
<b>knowledge and progress.</b>

72
00:05:18.666 --> 00:05:25.208
<b>And their antidote is humility and curiosity.</b>

73
00:05:25.208 --> 00:05:26.583
<b>Humility -</b>

74
00:05:26.583 --> 00:05:30.333
<b>will keep ego and envy away,</b>

75
00:05:30.333 --> 00:05:31.916
<b>and curiosity -</b>

76
00:05:31.916 --> 00:05:37.916
<b>will be helpful in finding answers to</b>
<b>questions by removing disbelief,</b>

77
00:05:37.916 --> 00:05:42.583
<b>it will encourage you to increase your abilities.</b>

78
00:05:42.583 --> 00:05:44.708
<b>Remember that</b>

79
00:05:44.708 --> 00:05:50.500
<b>in the face of the mysteries </b>
<b>and vastness of this universe,</b>

80
00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:53.291
<b>we are insignificant.</b>

81
00:05:53.291 --> 00:05:54.208
<b>And</b>

82
00:05:54.208 --> 00:05:58.041
<b>this is the beauty of it,</b>

83
00:05:58.041 --> 00:06:00.458
<b>if everything was known,</b>

84
00:06:00.458 --> 00:06:04.625
<b>everything was seen or known,</b>

85
00:06:04.625 --> 00:06:07.875
<b>wouldn't life become dull?</b>

86
00:06:07.875 --> 00:06:13.291
<b>There is so much to know, so much to do.</b>

87
00:06:13.291 --> 00:06:14.958
<b>Keep moving forward,</b>

88
00:06:14.958 --> 00:06:18.416
<b>just as this universe is infinite,</b>

89
00:06:18.416 --> 00:06:21.750
<b>you also have infinite potential.</b>

90
00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:23.791
<b>But yes,</b>

91
00:06:23.791 --> 00:06:25.416
<b>in this journey,</b>

92
00:06:25.416 --> 00:06:28.333
<b>humility and curiosity,</b>

93
00:06:28.333 --> 00:06:33.000
<b>always remember these two basic mantras.</b>

94
00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:43.125
<b>I remember all the things of infinite ages and eras.</b>

95
00:06:43.125 --> 00:06:46.291
<b>I remember the creation of this universe,</b>

96
00:06:46.291 --> 00:06:51.375
<b>I remember my knowledge given</b>
<b>to the sun god Vivasvan.</b>

97
00:06:51.375 --> 00:06:52.625
<b>And now</b>

98
00:06:52.625 --> 00:06:59.583
<b>I am here imparting this same </b>
<b>spiritual truth to Arjuna.</b>

99
00:06:59.583 --> 00:07:00.791
<b>But</b>

100
00:07:00.791 --> 00:07:03.625
<b>the main thing here is that</b>

101
00:07:03.625 --> 00:07:04.708
<b>Arjuna</b>

102
00:07:04.708 --> 00:07:09.208
<b>is also eager to learn all this from me.</b>

103
00:07:09.208 --> 00:07:11.000
<b>In the family environment,</b>

104
00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:17.791
<b>you also have many experienced, many elderly </b>
<b>people in front of you. </b>

105
00:07:17.791 --> 00:07:27.416
<b>Such people who have seen far more situations, </b>
<b>successes/failures and changes than you.</b>

106
00:07:27.416 --> 00:07:36.125
<b>And it is by seeing all this that their life</b>
<b>experience has become so mature.</b>

107
00:07:36.125 --> 00:07:38.000
<b>But many times,</b>

108
00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:39.250
<b>in families,</b>

109
00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:45.458
<b>the experience and wisdom </b>
<b>of such elders is ignored.</b>

110
00:07:45.458 --> 00:07:48.500
<b>Their thinking is declared old,</b>

111
00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:50.166
<b>and in the modern era,</b>

112
00:07:50.166 --> 00:07:53.208
<b>it is rendered useless.</b>

113
00:07:53.208 --> 00:07:56.583
<b>Their words go unheard.</b>

114
00:07:56.583 --> 00:07:58.625
<b>Remember,</b>

115
00:07:58.625 --> 00:08:07.000
<b>if we want, we will get a perspective </b>
<b>from their stories and anecdotes,</b>

116
00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:12.416
<b>which will both caution us and encourage us.</b>

117
00:08:12.416 --> 00:08:13.958
<b>But</b>

118
00:08:13.958 --> 00:08:16.625
<b>the youth want to run fast,</b>

119
00:08:16.625 --> 00:08:21.291
<b>these things seem like an obstacle to them.</b>

120
00:08:21.291 --> 00:08:24.458
<b>And this is where the mistake happens.</b>

121
00:08:24.458 --> 00:08:29.791
<b>Being cautious is not an obstacle or hindrance.</b>

122
00:08:29.791 --> 00:08:33.041
<b>Understand this with this example,</b>

123
00:08:33.041 --> 00:08:36.291
<b>today's vehicles have brakes.</b>

124
00:08:36.291 --> 00:08:39.375
<b>What is the purpose of this brake?</b>

125
00:08:39.375 --> 00:08:44.625
<b>Someone will say that the purpose </b>
<b>of this brake is to stop the vehicle</b>

126
00:08:44.625 --> 00:08:48.291
<b>or slow down its speed.</b>

127
00:08:48.291 --> 00:08:49.250
<b>Now</b>

128
00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:53.250
<b>think from a different perspective,</b>

129
00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:55.958
<b>if there were no brakes,</b>

130
00:08:55.958 --> 00:09:01.875
<b>could you drive your vehicle </b>
<b>at high speed? No, right?</b>

131
00:09:01.875 --> 00:09:05.666
<b>Because doing so would cause an accident.</b>

132
00:09:05.666 --> 00:09:12.333
<b>It is because of the brakes in your vehicle </b>
<b>that you are able to drive it at high speed.</b>

133
00:09:12.333 --> 00:09:17.500
<b>Because you know that now </b>
<b>there is no fear of an accident,</b>

134
00:09:17.500 --> 00:09:19.333
<b>when the road is bad</b>

135
00:09:19.333 --> 00:09:22.166
<b>or there is an obstacle ahead,</b>

136
00:09:22.166 --> 00:09:25.000
<b>you can slow down your vehicle,</b>

137
00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:30.625
<b>and as soon as the obstacle is removed, </b>
<b>you can move forward at high speed again.</b>

138
00:09:30.625 --> 00:09:32.291
<b>If you look at it,</b>

139
00:09:32.291 --> 00:09:37.250
<b>having brakes gives you the </b>
<b>courage to increase your speed.</b>

140
00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:40.583
<b>The knowledge of the elders is also like this.</b>

141
00:09:40.583 --> 00:09:41.958
<b>Their experiences,</b>

142
00:09:41.958 --> 00:09:47.583
<b>their alerting you, is in your interest,</b>

143
00:09:47.583 --> 00:09:51.041
<b>so that you progress at a fast pace,</b>

144
00:09:51.041 --> 00:09:56.125
<b>and at the same time avoid accidents.</b>

145
00:09:56.125 --> 00:10:02.833
<b>So ignoring/not listening to this knowledge </b>
<b>of theirs is a mistake, isn't it?</b>

146
00:10:02.833 --> 00:10:09.375
<b>Whether to use brakes or not while driving </b>
<b>a vehicle is in your hands,</b>

147
00:10:09.375 --> 00:10:13.666
<b>but having brakes in the vehicle </b>
<b>is very necessary.</b>

148
00:10:13.666 --> 00:10:15.708
<b>Similarly,</b>

149
00:10:15.708 --> 00:10:19.208
<b>your life, your pace is yours.</b>

150
00:10:19.208 --> 00:10:24.708
<b>Now whether you will use the suggestions </b>
<b>given by the elders on this path or not,</b>

151
00:10:24.708 --> 00:10:26.916
<b>it is up to you,</b>

152
00:10:26.916 --> 00:10:27.708
<b>but</b>

153
00:10:27.708 --> 00:10:35.041
<b>always keeping their knowledge with you, </b>
<b>this is extremely important.</b>

154
00:10:35.041 --> 00:10:39.250
<b>Now how to do this in a practical way?</b>

155
00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:43.166
<b>By spending regular time with </b>
<b>the elders of the family,</b>

156
00:10:43.166 --> 00:10:45.250
<b>by discussing with them,</b>

157
00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:46.916
<b>by asking them questions,</b>

158
00:10:46.916 --> 00:10:49.791
<b>by listening to their perspective.</b>

159
00:10:49.791 --> 00:10:56.333
<b>The time spent like this will not only give you </b>
<b>the gift of their invaluable experience,</b>

160
00:10:56.333 --> 00:10:57.958
<b>but at the same time</b>

161
00:10:57.958 --> 00:11:02.250
<b>it will also strengthen the family affection.</b>

162
00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:05.250
<b>When the elders of the family see</b>

163
00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:14.041
<b>that their experiences are being respected, </b>
<b>they will also feel joy.</b>

164
00:11:14.041 --> 00:11:16.958
<b>How beautiful is this imagination,</b>

165
00:11:16.958 --> 00:11:24.083
<b>where the elders and the younger ones of </b>
<b>the family lovingly discuss some subject,</b>

166
00:11:24.083 --> 00:11:28.000
<b>respect each other.</b>

167
00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:32.291
<b>Think about this perspective.</b>

168
00:11:36.625 --> 00:11:43.708
<b>Standing in the middle of the Mahabharata war </b>
<b>at Kurukshetra, Arjuna</b>

169
00:11:43.708 --> 00:11:53.750
<b>is trying to solve the tangle of his life with </b>
<b>my knowledge and my teachings.</b>

170
00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:56.375
<b>In a professional environment,</b>

171
00:11:56.375 --> 00:12:02.958
<b>you too must get stuck in some tangle </b>
<b>or trouble many times?</b>

172
00:12:02.958 --> 00:12:06.125
<b>Look around you,</b>

173
00:12:06.125 --> 00:12:13.000
<b>you will find many such people who</b>
<b>have been in that business for decades,</b>

174
00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:18.125
<b>who have been working in </b>
<b>that organization for a long time.</b>

175
00:12:18.125 --> 00:12:19.916
<b>Such individuals have </b>

176
00:12:19.916 --> 00:12:29.708
<b>a store of deep knowledge and important </b>
<b>experience related to the organization or business</b>

177
00:12:29.708 --> 00:12:31.083
<b>Education</b>

178
00:12:31.083 --> 00:12:34.750
<b>and academic degrees are essential.</b>

179
00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:38.625
<b>They provide knowledge to the youth,</b>

180
00:12:38.625 --> 00:12:40.000
<b>but</b>

181
00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:49.291
<b>there are some things that only experience </b>
<b>and time can teach you.</b>

182
00:12:49.291 --> 00:12:53.666
<b>These people have that priceless education. </b>

183
00:12:53.666 --> 00:12:59.916
<b>Do not make the mistake of ignoring the</b>
<b>understanding of such experienced people.</b>

184
00:12:59.916 --> 00:13:04.583
<b>Just as Arjuna is eager to learn from me,</b>

185
00:13:04.583 --> 00:13:05.750
<b>you too</b>

186
00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:10.916
<b>awaken this desire to learn within yourself.</b>

187
00:13:10.916 --> 00:13:13.291
<b>Learn from the senior officials of the organization,</b>

188
00:13:13.291 --> 00:13:17.000
<b>and people who have been working for years,</b>

189
00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:19.625
<b>spend time with them,</b>

190
00:13:19.625 --> 00:13:22.208
<b>take advice from them.</b>

191
00:13:22.208 --> 00:13:28.375
<b>And it is also in the interest of the organization </b>
<b>to encourage such an environment.</b>

192
00:13:28.375 --> 00:13:32.416
<b>How can this be done in a practical way?</b>

193
00:13:32.416 --> 00:13:35.166
<b>There are many ways to do this.</b>

194
00:13:35.166 --> 00:13:39.833
<b>Groups should be formed to work on projects,</b>

195
00:13:39.833 --> 00:13:46.375
<b>which include some experienced people </b>
<b>and senior officials along with the youth.</b>

196
00:13:46.375 --> 00:13:50.458
<b>An education tradition can also be established</b>

197
00:13:50.458 --> 00:13:58.125
<b>where every new employee has to regularly </b>
<b>spend time with an experienced employee,</b>

198
00:13:58.125 --> 00:14:01.416
<b>work under them.</b>

199
00:14:01.416 --> 00:14:02.875
<b>By doing so,</b>

200
00:14:02.875 --> 00:14:07.583
<b>young employees will get </b>
<b>the benefit of experience,</b>

201
00:14:07.583 --> 00:14:09.750
<b>but at the same time,</b>

202
00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:14.500
<b>old employees will also get a sense </b>
<b>of their unique importance,</b>

203
00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:19.541
<b>and they will also learn some </b>
<b>new things from the youth.</b>

204
00:14:19.541 --> 00:14:21.916
<b>This is what an organization needs</b>

205
00:14:21.916 --> 00:14:26.500
<b>Such an environment. Such a harmony.</b>

206
00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:32.500
<b>Where there is youthful enthusiasm, and the </b>
<b>experience of senior colleagues.</b>

207
00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:35.458
<b>Such an environment will be invaluable.</b>

208
00:14:35.458 --> 00:14:39.250
<b>Create it in your organization.</b>

